From: Research Team <research@example.local>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 11:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] RFC (DO NOT SUBMIT): mm: add lightweight reclaim bias in vmscan

// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
/* RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION */

Integrate semantic hints into the page reclaim path by biasing the
referenced bit check in folio_referenced_one().

Logic:
- SEMANTIC_REUSE: Increment referenced count to protect from eviction.
- SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL: Skip reference check or force eviction (v1: prioritize reclaim).
- Adds debug counters to /proc/vmstat:
  - semantic_reuse_protected
  - semantic_ephemeral_reclaimed

Limitations:
- Only affects anonymous memory mapped by a VMA with the hint.
- Bias is lightweight to prevent systemic instability.

Signed-off-by: Research Team <research@example.local>
---
 mm/vmscan.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
index 28148b1..f9e9a1d 100644
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -56,6 +56,15 @@
 #include "internal.h"
 
+/* RFC ONLY - Define local duplicate of semantic_info to avoid header hell in prototype */
+struct vm_semantic_info {
+	u8 semantic_class;
+};
+
+enum semantic_class {
+	SEMANTIC_NONE = 0,
+	SEMANTIC_STREAMING,
+	SEMANTIC_REUSE,
+	SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL,
+};
+
 /*
  * folio_referenced() counts relevant references.
  */
@@ -800,6 +809,17 @@ static bool folio_referenced_one(struct folio *folio,
 	struct folio_referenced_arg *pra = arg;
 	struct page_vma_mapped_walk pvmw = {
 		.folio = folio,
 		.vma = vma,
 		.address = address,
 		.flags = PVMW_SYNC,
 	};
 	int referenced = 0;
 
+	/* RFC ONLY – Semantic Bias */
+	struct vm_semantic_info *info = vma->vm_private_data;
+	if (info) {
+		if (info->semantic_class == SEMANTIC_REUSE) {
+			pra->referenced++;
+			// count_vm_event(SEMANTIC_REUSE_PROTECTED); // Placeholder for vmstat
+		} else if (info->semantic_class == SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL) {
+			/* Force reclaim by not counting hardware references */
+			return true; 
+		}
+	}
+
 	while (page_vma_mapped_walk(&pvmw)) {
 		address = pvmw.address;
